WEBVTT

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.730 --> 00:02:02.150
The Duelist
Chapter IV

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.450
In the early winter of Imperial Year 483...

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.390
...the event on Odin which had attracted the attention of the aristocrats...

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:17.650
...the dispute between the Helksheimers and the Schafhausens...

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.680
...ended in a draw as a result of
Kaiser Friedrich IV's intervention.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.550
Though there were those who
were satisfied with the outcome...

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:31.220
...it cannot be denied that
many more were discontented.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:39.080
Oh, don't be so upset,
Count Helksheimer.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.740
We cannot oppose an
Imperial order openly.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:44.450
Since you gained half,
you should be content.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.850
My lord Marquis seems to be modest.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.730
Don't be so sarcastic.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:55.610
Since you've secured half the rights,
we can take the rest any way we can.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.110
Is that so ?

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.900
Well, just leave it to me.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:06.850
Eventually, there will be nothing
in this Empire that I cannot obtain.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.140
He's late !

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.230
It's been ten days.{the duel}
What is he doing ?

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.830
I cannot wait any longer.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.750
Yes, well...

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:33.230
But that man was
injured in the duel.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:38.270
Moreover, it was the shoulder of his dominant arm, and the bullet reached the bone...

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.090
...it's really tricky.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:40.900
Such rubbish !

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.990
Yes, Madam...

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.210
You're a doctor, aren't you ?

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:49.270
Why don't you fix it ?

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:55.730
Ah, well, but if I get in direct contact
with him, it might be rather inconvenient...

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:00.020
If he can't be depended upon, 
you should get rid of him quickly.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.880
Get someone else.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.160
It can't be done that easily.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.470
Such an appropriate
character is hard to find, so...

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:13.890
But the longer it takes, the greater
the chances our secret may leak out.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.550
I can't wait.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.600
If he acts quickly, then fine.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.230
But if not, just get rid 
of him immediately !

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.750
P...please, be patient just for now...

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.550
I'll have him finish
the job in a day or two...

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:29.880
Are you positive ?

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.360
You're sure, aren't you ?

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.930
Y...yes.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.850
Then fine.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.680
But either way, 
prepare to silence him.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.480
Understood ?

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.950
Yes, Madam.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:45.970
Yes...

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:56.100
In February, Reinhard's
wound had almost healed.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.850
But the wound to his pride
might have been more serious.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.570
Kircheis...

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.480
...how hopelessly powerless I am...

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:17.850
It's something I started in order to
help my sister, even just indirectly.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.000
But in the end, 
she saved me...

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:27.360
...and when I think that she even
had to plead to that man to save me...

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:32.920
Try not to think about it too much.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.210
Your wound is almost healed.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:49.300
I suppose it's a byproduct of war that surgical techniques have made such immense advancements.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.510
It's fortunate that the
bullet didn't reach the bone.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:00.300
In a month or so, there'll be
no trace of the injury left.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:05.340
Yeah, sorry to trouble you as always.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.230
He's really depressed.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.270
I'm heading out to the
Ministry of the Military.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.140
Yeah, go ahead.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:20.550
"Since I am dissatisfied with the outcome of our earlier duel..."

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:23.900
"...I would like to settle the affair without outside intervention."

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.300
"Time and place are..."

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.230
That's it.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:50.270
If I can at least win this fight, that might lift some of this gloom over my feelings.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:56.410
Because I couldn't defeat that bastard,
I ended up letting the Kaiser intervene.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.500
Only if I have the power to
win any and all battles...

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:17.090
What kind of excuse
should I give Kircheis ?

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:37.540
Lord Reinhard, what happened ?

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.170
Sorry about this.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:42.390
I was a bit irritated and
accidentally broke the window.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:44.170
I'll take care of it.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:46.660
Lord Reinhard, please
relax and leave it to me.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.320
It's strange.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.500
The glass shards are
scattered inside the room.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.060
It seems the window was
broken from the outside, but...

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:14.100
Oh, Lord Reinhard, 
did you move the picture ?

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:16.140
Huh ?

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.880
Yeah, I just thought
I'd change the mood.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.380
I see.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.710
Something must have happened.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:29.220
By the way, Kircheis, make
some time for me tomorrow.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.250
What are you planning to do ?

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.300
I want to have some fencing practice.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.710
Why so suddenly ?

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:41.220
After that duel earlier,
I realized I need more training.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:44.360
I want to gain enough skill
to protect myself, at least.

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:49.360
Besides, unless I get some
exercise in, I'll only get gloomier.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:04.610
Starting the next day, Reinhard began practicing his fencing with Kircheis.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:10.200
Furthermore, he also started 
researching the art of sword fighting.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:13.930
How is it going ?

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:17.190
Did you find anything useful ?

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:18.320
Yeah.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.950
When swords were meaningful 
as a weapon in actual combat...

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:25.680
...it was back in the era the humans were still confined to Earth.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.100
Till around the
19th century A.D., it seems.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:31.630
19th century, that means...

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.750
...1,700 years ago ?

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:41.950
Even before that, a country in the East had many different schools of swordsmanship.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.950
And those schools competed with one another to perfect their style.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:48.850
That's a characteristic
not found in other regions.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:00.550
Within the perfected styles
of those various schools...

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.390
...I wonder if there is a deathblow attack for actual combat.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:10.950
As I thought, Lord Reinhard seems to be intent on fighting that man.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.850
I wonder if he initiated the challenge ?

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:19.910
Either way, why
is he so persistent ?

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:22.230
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.340
I'm glad you came.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.400
I want a satisfactory
conclusion to our fight as well.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:36.450
But I want to know one thing.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:39.500
You're not just a duelist, are you ?

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.740
I believe you're an assassin sent by
the Marchioness Benemunde, correct ?

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.610
I don't know about that.

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:54.200
As a duelist, I can't get any more jobs
after a fight like that, so I need closure.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:55.550
That's all there is to it.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.700
All right then.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.880
There's no need
for further discussion.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.000
Draw !

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:34.460
I knew this was 
what was happening.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.790
Lord Reinhard...!

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.450
It may be called despicable...

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:49.380
...and Lord Reinhard may scold me,
but I won't risk his death in a fight like this.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:53.010
Depending on the situation, I may have to kill his opponent myself...

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:57.080
Then let's begin.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.350
His sword is slow.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:06.150
His shoulder doesn't seem
to be completely healed.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:18.470
Whoa !{means "stop" for the horse, I think}

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:21.570
Whoa !{ditto}

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:24.650
Yah ! {means "go" for the horse, I think}

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:34.000
Then why hasten this rematch ?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.780
Couldn't he have challenged me after his injury was healed...?

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:50.250
He really must be working
under someone's orders.

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:51.840
That's why he's rushing to fight me...

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:55.600
Whoa, whoa !{"stop" for the horse}

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:02.300
If we fight in this manner, he cannot use the sword with his left hand.

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:04.950
That means he's aiming for...

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:15.970
That bastard - he must be
aiming for Lord Reinhard...

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:46.170
As I thought, he's led
us to a ground battle.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:49.210
But it doesn't change the fact of his disadvantage in not being able to use his right hand.

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:56.400
Don't think I'm still the
same as I was before !

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:01.200
This fight is over.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.820
I presume you have
no further complaints ?

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:17.740
Leave this place and never
come before me again !

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:56.100
Why take such a meaningless action ?

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:08.090
Once I'm defeated by an amateur,
I can't continue to live as a duelist...

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.450
Spit it out.

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:12.100
Who's your client ?

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:16.810
There's no such thing...

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:18.620
It's a matter of my pride...

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:30.270
I'll pretend that was the case.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.110
Take your secret
along with you to hell.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:52.760
Such a worrywart...

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:21.390
Welcome home, Lord Reinhard.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:24.530
Oh, you're up already.

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:27.170
Where were you off to
so early in the morning ?

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.740
It's nothing.

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:34.960
Oh yeah, since it was cold outside,
the gloves you gave me came in handy.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:38.990
I'm glad.

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:42.450
They're made of the material
that's used in protective suits...

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:44.300
...but they guard against
the cold as well ?

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:45.950
Yeah.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:48.450
I just made coffee.

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.240
Lord Reinhard, would you like some ?

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:52.900
Oh, that sounds good.

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:55.140
I was getting cold.

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:00.870
Please.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.150
Yeah, thanks.

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:17.400
Lord Reinhard.

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:18.630
What is it ?

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:21.700
Please try not to be too reckless.

00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:25.170
Your life is not yours alone.

00:22:36.650 --> 00:22:37.480
Yeah.

00:22:41.300 --> 00:22:44.890
The background of this affair remained in the darkness.

00:22:44.890 --> 00:22:53.240
But it certainly seems to have made the bond between Reinhard and Kircheis even stronger.

00:22:53.240 --> 00:22:58.700
Needless to say, this incident had
no effect on Reinhard's rise in rank.

